# Line endings for files that must stay byte-identical across machines.
#
# The failure this prevents: `git archive` on a Windows checkout with the
# default core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into the tarball, so on the Linux box
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash` + `set -euo pipefail` dies with "invalid option name"
# and every Python shebang script carries a stray \r.  Marking these paths as
# LF in the repository makes the archive export LF regardless of local config.
#
# Binary artifacts are declared so git never tries to normalise them.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.csv           text eol=lf
*.ini           text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt  text eol=lf
*.cmake         text eol=lf
*.bat           text eol=crlf

*.bin           binary
*.png           binary
*.zip           binary
